  "claim": {
    "anchor": "Ametista do Sul, Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil — amethyst geodes in the Serra Geral Formation high-Ti basalt (Paraná Continental Flood Basalt Province, Lower Cretaceous ~134 Ma)",
    "description": "A Brazilian amethyst geode. A basalt gas cavity fills inward — celadonite rim → agate → clear quartz → amethyst. Mid-growth a green celadonite film frosts the amethyst prism faces; the tip renews a wider cap THROUGH the film — a MASKING SCEPTRE (the non-corrosive masking counterpart to grimsel's corrosion sceptre). Goethite staining at the base.",
    "expects_species": [
      "chalcedony",
      "quartz"
    ],
    "expectation_contract": {
      "deterministic": [
        {
          "mineral": "chalcedony",
          "reason": "Authored headline release promise.",
